Upstream credit (from the file's own header)
--------------------------------------------
The construction is Tom Wambsgans' leanSphincs candidate crate
(TomWambsgans/leanXMSS-leanSPHINCS-candidates, crates/sphincs on branch keccak,
MIT OR Apache-2.0; itself adapted from leanVM's SPHINCS crate). No upstream code
is copied: the signer is written from the specs, cross-checked against the Rust
ports and the on-chain verifiers.

Why vendored here
-----------------
This is the authoritative Python signer for leanSphincs-s over Ethereum
Keccak-256. The testbed prefers it over the repository's Rust binary so the
leanSphincs PoC stays pip-only: it depends only on pycryptodome
(Crypto.Hash.keccak), already in the testbed's requirements.txt. It matches the
on-chain verifier src/keccak/LeanSphincs-SAsm.sol
(verify(bytes32 pkSeed, bytes32 pkRoot, bytes32 message, bytes sig)).

Treat as read-only, like the other core/vendor/ engines. Not audited, not
production-safe.
